[length:03:18]
[ti:Emerald Girl]
[ar:Aracne]
[al:Chaotic-Disfuntyonal]
[au:Aracne]
[lr:Aracne]
[by:Aracne]
[re:LRC Workbench by Azaria (lrc-workbench.azariadev.dev)]
[ve:0.3.2]
[00:04.44]She walks in cherry smoke and glitter pink
[00:09.02]cat-eyed martyr with tired lipstick on her skin
[00:12.65]crow on one shoulder / roses on the other
[00:16.17]smiling like a goddess
[00:18.39]born with stakes beneath her velvet
[00:21.07]Amber fire shining softly through her lashes
[00:24.10]plastic crooked halo glowing pale and strange
[00:28.10]quiet like thunder sleeping under silk sheets
[00:31.84]born with wild green secrets
[00:33.77]hidden underneath the pain
[00:36.39]She paints her mouth with holy water lipstick
[00:39.90]just to survive another day in hell
[00:43.47]wears gold around the places life once fractured
[00:47.21]porcelain mended softly
[00:49.27]where nobody can tell
[00:51.60]She smiles like spring
[00:53.21]but carries winter in her ribs
[00:54.97]keeps little wings between her bones
[00:56.97]for the day she finally slips
[00:59.09]free from gravity’s fingers
[01:00.99]free from rooms that never heal
[01:03.01]still she blooms in neon gardens
[01:04.87]making broken things look real
[01:06.72]They only see the glitter
[01:09.07]never how she defies gravity
[01:10.61]few know the green fire
[01:12.12]blooming under bruised silk quietly
[01:14.37]They call her lovely
[01:15.79]because she hides the storm so well
[01:19.09]but saints with sharpened roses
[01:20.59]learn to build a home inside a hell
[01:23.34]Quiet girl
[01:25.12]emerald heart
[01:26.57]plastic crooked halo
[01:27.94]tilted from the start
[01:30.12]pink outside
[01:31.96]green where it scars
[01:35.20]quiet girl…
[01:36.65]born beneath emerald stars
[01:39.00]Quiet girl
[01:40.65]velvet spark
[01:41.81]holy mouth / hidden venom
[01:43.99]soft inside the dark
[01:45.94]crow and rose
[01:47.40]thorn and art
[01:50.51]quiet girl…
[01:51.97]keeper of a fearless heart
[01:55.46]Two little shadows curl in moonlit corners
[01:58.96]soft-eyed witnesses to nights she never names
[02:02.26]her house—a tender chaos made of bright things
[02:05.65]half-finished little kingdoms
[02:07.54]lit by soft domestic fires
[02:10.34]She makes a home
[02:12.01]where tender things are taught to ache
[02:13.58]still sets the table beautifully
[02:15.12]for hearts that bend but do not break
[02:17.17]amber eyes lit like candles
[02:19.41]laughing bright through tired bones
[02:21.36]wearing all her sweetest colors
[02:23.22]while she carries hurt alone
[02:26.77]Soft hands teaching serpents how to sleep
[02:29.49]gentle enough to hold the dark without sinking in too deep
[02:34.12]stone-seed center
[02:35.44]secret green
[02:37.30]a prophecy unseen
[02:38.17]a wild heart wrapped in velvet pink
[02:40.95]stronger than she’s ever seemed
[02:43.00]And when the night grows teeth around her
[02:46.69]when the walls begin to close
[02:49.87]still she rises / bright and painted
[02:53.22]with a springtime in her throat
[02:57.16]Quiet girl
[03:04.25]keeper of a fearless heart
[03:08.71]One day she’ll fly away
[03:11.48]One day she finally do it.
